Title: Memories of Cirencester's Old Station sought for history festival
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Jess Yarrow', 'Text': '"We know that there are lots of people out there who can remember the station in its heyday," said Ms Yarrow.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 83}}, {'Speaker': 'Jess Yarrow', 'Text': '"We\'d love to hear stories, we\'d love to see photographs, we\'d love to have any memorabilia that people have got tucked away because we\'ll be dressing the station as if it were a station with prams and benches and cases, so anything like that people have, we\'d love to know about it."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 239}}, {'Speaker': 'Jonathan Rixon', 'Text': 'The building holds many hidden treasures, including a boardroom where Brunel sought a meeting space outside London.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 15, 'EndChar': 112}}, {'Speaker': 'Jonathan Rixon', 'Text': '"It\'s important to protect our industrial heritage. I\'m passionate about preserving this piece of history and sharing it with the town."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 135}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'A history festival is calling for memories of a former railway station, which will be temporarily reopened during the event.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 95}}, {'Description': 'Cirencester History Festival takes place from 25 October to 1 November, offering talks and activities on local and global history.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 107}}, {'Description': "People will be able to tour the town's Grade-II listed Old Station, which was designed by Isambard Kingdom Brunel and closed in 1965.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Description': 'The free event on both Saturdays of the festival will celebrate the "golden age of rail," said festival producer Jess Yarrow.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 111}}, {'Description': 'Ms Yarrow said most people know the Old Station as "a slightly sad, empty-looking building" but she hopes some will remember using it, on their commute, or even watching it welcome evacuees and soldiers during World War Two.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 204}}, {'Description': 'Architect Jonathan Rixon is refurbishing the station to use as his offices, and he will lead the tours.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 91}}, {'Description': 'There will also be an audio listening project sharing stories of the station, and Cirencester College students have worked with Mr Rixon to create a virtual reality experience of the station during the Victoria era.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 188}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'A black and white image of a steam train waiting on a platform while three men have their arms round each other smiling for a photo. They are wearing suits and hats, that look like they work at the station.'}]}
